{
  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_007 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, weighted) achieved 0.5232 acc, while config_002 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) achieved only 0.2079 acc. This large gap shows the RNA modality is critical, but we cannot yet decompose whether RNA alone drives most of the signal or whether there is genuine multimodal synergy. Uncertainty: We lack an RNA-only baseline to attribute performance to each modality. This experiment (config_019: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is a clean ablation of config_007 with the image removed, holding RNA encoder and profile setting constant. It will clarify: (a) if RNA alone ≈ 0.5, the image adds little and we should focus on RNA representation; (b) if RNA alone is much lower (~0.2-0.3), there is true multimodal synergy and fusion strategy becomes the key design axis. This is the best use of the next budget slot because it completes the fundamental modality decomposition (image_only / rna_only / multimodal) before investing in more complex configurations (multiprofile, different encoders, aggregation), ensuring subsequent experiments target the right design dimensions."
}

